P("The gauge data are from the PEGELONLINE",
  r"The gauge data are from the PEGELONLINE service of the German waterway administration \citep{pegelonline2026}, and the forecasts from the Federal Institute of Hydrology \citep{bfg2026fourteen,bfg2026}. The input--output table is the OECD ICIO 2025 edition \citep{oecd2025icio}. The transport network is the TEN-T network of the European Commission (TENtec). The facility data are the open trackers of Global Energy Monitor, Climate TRACE, and SPAM 2020, and the employment data are the Eurostat regional accounts. The inventory durations are from the Bundesbank corporate balance-sheet statistics and the sources of Supplementary Section~S1. The gauge profile, the monthly path of Supplementary Table~\ref{tab:prospective}, and the run tables of this paper are deposited on Zenodo at submission (Methods). The model's scope data package (network, agents, tables, and scenario files) will be deposited on Zenodo upon acceptance; until then, it is available from the corresponding author.")

P("DisruptSC is open source under",
  r"DisruptSC is open source under the \texttt{GPL-3.0} license at \url{https://github.com/ccolon/disrupt-sc}. The study scripts (scenario driver, batch job lists, analysis and figure scripts, the manuscript's number and table generators) are in \texttt{studies/rhine2026}. The release used for the submitted version will be tagged and archived on Zenodo with a DOI upon acceptance (\todo{tag the release, reserve the Zenodo DOI and write it here}). Until then, the repository's commit history provides the same code.")

